        {
          "id": "506192a1-1de0-3512-a166-05ecd3e716b5",
          "content": {
            "id": "506192a1-1de0-3512-a166-05ecd3e716b5",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Affordable Care Act: Lawmakers should target healthcare red tape",
            "description": "<p>As Republican lawmakers begin to align with House Democrats on extending Affordable Care Act (better known as Obamacare) subsidies, what is the general consensus among Americans on healthcare affordability?</p>\n<p>These ACA tax credits \u2014 which work to lower the cost of health insurance and reduce recipients' monthly premiums \u2014 are set to expire on December 31.</p>\n<p>Columbia University health policy professor Meghan Fitzgerald outlines how sharply healthcare costs and insurance fees will rise if these subsidies expire and why lawmakers should prioritize cutting down on waste and red tape for Americans to receive proper treatments.</p>\n<p>Fitzgerald is also Grey Ghost Capital's private equity investor, a board member of Tenet Healthcare, and a former nurse.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
            "summary": "As Republican lawmakers begin to align with House Democrats on extending Affordable Care Act (better known as Obamacare) subsidies, what is the general consensus among Americans on healthcare affordability? These ACA tax credits \u2014 which work to lower the cost of health insurance and reduce recipients' monthly premiums \u2014 are set to expire on December 31. Columbia University health policy professor Meghan Fitzgerald outlines how sharply healthcare costs and insurance fees will rise if these subsidies expire and why lawmakers should prioritize cutting down on waste and red tape for Americans to receive proper treatments. Fitzgerald is also Grey Ghost Capital's private equity investor, a board member of Tenet Healthcare, and a former nurse. To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more&nbsp;Market Catalysts.",
